From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:02:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/41] USB MIDI: no more lost packets when the computer sends
 faster than once per millisecond (upstream b93a9cfc)

As a USB device, the Deluge re-arms a MIDI receive only when the task scheduler polls it,
about once per millisecond. Meanwhile the hardware kept acknowledging incoming packets; one that
arrived before the re-arm was thrown away after the computer had already seen it acknowledged.
Dense MIDI from a DAW and SysEx (the SD access over USB, v7) lost packets or crawled.

Now the pipe is set to NAK once a transfer is in, so the computer retries until the next re-arm;
every packet already in the double-buffered FIFO is drained into a receive buffer of 192 instead
of 64 bytes; an empty or mismatched FIFO reopens the pipe instead of forcing termination.
Only the device side (USB to a computer), as upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
